title: IntroductionPart1
---
<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: 34... 36... there we go, 38! and the apartment number was...

chip: 20. cool.

<<empty characterSprite>>
narrator: you push the "20" button on the panel next to the door and within seconds you hear a buzz.

<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: damn, okay, that was fast.

<<empty characterSprite>>
narrator: the front door of the apartment building unlocks with a nice, crisp click and with that, you push it open.

narrator: now that you're inside, there's nothing that particularly catches your attention about this place, definitely not upon first glance.

narrator: there are a bunch of taiga packages lying around the mailroom, layers of dust caking the staircase...

narrator: the usual. it's like looking at a copy of your own building's lobby, kinda.

narrator: speaking of stairs, though... what floor was this guy on again? you walk a little further into the hallway a ways in from the lobby.

<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: elevator...?

<<empty characterSprite>>
narrator: nope. tough luck, you're taking the stairs.

<<chipNeutral characterSprite>>
chip: fuck. fine.

<<empty characterSprite>>
narrator: begrudgingly, you ascend the six flights of stairs and wind up face to face with apartment 20.

narrator: before you even get a chance to knock, you notice the door is cracked just a hair. so, naturally, you push it open.

<<luciBack characterSprite>>
lucifer: hey! oh wow, i didn't think you'd get here this quickly!   

<<luciNeutral characterSprite>>
lucifer: um... yeah, make yourself at home. i didn't really get the chance to clean up much before you got here but...
 
lucifer: i hope that's alright. it's not that bad, just messy. you know how it is.

<<chipPeace characterSprite>>
chip: yeah, that's alright.


